{"id":"word:hebrew:H2689","type":"word","title":"חֲצֹצְרָה","subtitle":"H2689 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"a trumpet (from its sundered or quavering note)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to חֲצֹצְרָה (H2689) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-f.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 29 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"חֲצֹצְרָה (chătsôtsᵉrâh) means a trumpet (from its sundered or quavering note) First listed occurrence: 1Chr 13 8."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"חֲצֹצְרָה","transliteration":"chătsôtsᵉrâh","pronunciation":"khats-o-tser-aw'","strong":"H2689","lemmaId":"hebrew:H2689","partOfSpeech":"n-f","forms":["בַּ/חֲצֹצְרֽוֹת","בַּ/חֲצֹ֣צְר֔וֹת","וּ/בַ/חֲצֹצְר֖וֹת","וַ/חֲצֹצְר֥וֹת","בַּ/חֲצֹצְר֑וֹת"],"morphs":[["HR/Ncfpa",14],["HC/R/Ncfpa",4],["HC/Td/Ncfpa",4],["HNcfpa",2],["HC/Ncfpc",2],["HRd/Ncfpa",1],["HNcfsa",1],["HNcfpc",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"a trumpet (from its sundered or quavering note)","usage":"trumpet(-er).","full":"H2689. chatsotsrah חֲצֹצְרָה noun feminine clarion (Late Hebrew חֲצוֺצֶרֶת , Aramaic חֲצוֺצַרְתָּצ ) — mostly P and late; — absolute ׳ח Hosea 5:8 ; plural absolute חֲצֹצְרוֺת Num 10:8 22 t.; חֲצֹצְרֹת 10:9-10 , construct id. 31:6 ; 2Chr 13:12 ; חֲצוֺצְרֹת Num 10:2 ; clarion: 1 as secular instr . Hosea 5:8 (|| שׁוֺפָר ) 2Kin 11:14 (twice in verse) = 2Chr 23:13 (twice in verse). 2 as sacred instr . 2Kin 12:14 , especially for use by priests (only P, Psalm 98 and Chronicles). a. בח ׳תקע (of blowing a single long blast) Num 10:3-4 , 7 , 8 , to gather congregation or ׳נשׂיא together, and, on festivals, over sacrifice, 'to be remembered before ׳י ,' 10:10 . b. בח תרועה ׳תקע , or בח ׳הריע (of sounding alarm, — a series of quick blasts) for camps to move Num 10:5-6 , also in battle, 10:9 , 'to be remembered before ׳י ;' so 31:6 ; 2Chr 13:12 (compare 13:14 ), both ׳ח התרועה . c. especially in Chr's descriptions of ceremonies at festivals, to express rejoicing: 1Chr 13:8 ; 15:28 (|| שׁוֺפָר קוֺל ), 16:6 , 42 ; 2Chr 15:14 (|| שׁוֺפָר ), 20:28 ; 29:26-27 , Ezra 3:10 ; Neh 12:35 , 41 ; Psa 98:6 (|| שׁוֺפָר קוֺל ); בח קוֺל ׳הָרִים 2Chr 5:13 ; בח ׳מחצצרים 1Chr 15:24 ; 2Chr 5:12-13 , 13:14 ; in 29:28 this participle agrees with noun in sense , and is masculine; and the clarions (= players on the clarions) sounded . — The חֲצֹצְרָה , or (sacred) clarion, was a long, straight, slender metal tube, with flaring end, see Benz Archäol. 277 ; distinguished thus from the שׁוֺפָר which was originally a ram's horn, and probably always retained the horn-shape; the שׁוֺפָר is mentioned constantly in the earlier literature, and was used by watchmen, warriors, etc., as well as priests (see Benz ib. 276 and שׁוֺפָר ).","rootNote":"by reduplication from 2690 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 13 8","keyReferences":["1Chr 13 8","1Chr 15 24","1Chr 15 28","1Chr 16 6","1Chr 16 42","2Chr 5 12","2Chr 5 13","2Chr 13 12"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":29,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 13 8","book":"1Chr","chapter":13,"verse":8,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וּ/בַ/חֲצֹצְרֽוֹת","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/R/Ncfpa"},{"reference":"1Chr 15 24","book":"1Chr","chapter":15,"verse":24,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"בַּ/חֲצֹ֣צְר֔וֹת","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Ncfpa"},{"reference":"1Chr 15 28","book":"1Chr","chapter":15,"verse":28,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וּ/בַ/חֲצֹצְר֖וֹת","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/R/Ncfpa"},{"reference":"1Chr 16 6","book":"1Chr","chapter":16,"verse":6,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"בַּ/חֲצֹצְר֣וֹת","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Ncfpa"},{"reference":"1Chr 16 42","book":"1Chr","chapter":16,"verse":42,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"חֲצֹצְר֤וֹת","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcfpa"},{"reference":"2Chr 5 12","book":"2Chr","chapter":5,"verse":12,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"ב